From 724fca86a9b9fd7012f64888b2951879acaa41c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bui Quang Minh <minhquangbui99@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Jun 2021 21:34:39 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 0339/1444] UPSTREAM: bpf: Fix integer overflow in argument
 calculation for bpf_map_area_alloc

commit 7dd5d437c258bbf4cc15b35229e5208b87b8b4e0 upstream.

In 32-bit architecture, the result of sizeof() is a 32-bit integer so
the expression becomes the multiplication between 2 32-bit integer which
can potentially leads to integer overflow. As a result,
bpf_map_area_alloc() allocates less memory than needed.

Fix this by casting 1 operand to u64.

Fixes: 0d2c4f964050 ("bpf: Eliminate rlimit-based memory accounting for sockmap and sockhash maps")
Fixes: 99c51064fb06 ("devmap: Use bpf_map_area_alloc() for allocating hash buckets")
