From 4ed7b7d86c05204a3c679bd1a8583471724ab367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexei Starovoitov <ast@kernel.org>
Date: Mon, 28 Oct 2019 20:24:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 0518/1444] UPSTREAM: bpf: Enforce 'return 0' in BTF-enabled
 raw_tp programs

The return value of raw_tp programs is ignored by __bpf_trace_run()
that calls them. The verifier also allows any value to be returned.
For BTF-enabled raw_tp lets enforce 'return 0', so that return value
can be used for something in the future.

Change-Id: I6bce4c2bbfb2a3ca16bc53e5416d201d18407d1f
Signed-off-by: Alexei Starovoitov <ast@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Daniel Borkmann <daniel@iogearbox.net>
Acked-by: Andrii Nakryiko <andriin@fb.com>
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20191029032426.1206762-1-ast@kernel.org
---
 kernel/bpf/verifier.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
index be84bac29f07..8c3fe63ac5cf 100644
--- a/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
+++ b/kernel/bpf/verifier.c
@@ -6559,6 +6559,11 @@ static int check_return_code(struct bpf_verifier_env *env)
 	case BPF_PROG_TYPE_CGROUP_SYSCTL:
 	case BPF_PROG_TYPE_CGROUP_SOCKOPT:
 		break;
+	case BPF_PROG_TYPE_RAW_TRACEPOINT:
+		if (!env->prog->aux->attach_btf_id)
+			return 0;
+		range = tnum_const(0);
+		break;
 	default:
 		return 0;
 	}

